{"name":"Noble Cause","hex":"#990c0d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"noble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An aristocrat; one of aristocratic blood. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A medieval gold coin of England in the 14th and 15th centuries, usually valued at 6s 8d."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having honorable qualities; having moral eminence and freedom from anything petty, mean or dubious in conduct and character.","Grand; stately; magnificent; splendid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noble"},{"term":"cause","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The source of, or reason for, an event or action; that which produces or effects a result.","Sufficient reason."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set off an event or action; to bring about; to produce.","To actively produce as a result, by means of force or authority."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cause"}],"entries":[{"title":"Causality","blocks":[{"text":"Causality is an influence by which one event, process, state, or subject contributes to the production of another event, process, state, or object where the cause is at least partly responsible for the effect, and the effect is at least partly dependent on the cause. The cause of something may also be described as the reason behind the event or process."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Causality"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Herald_of_Free_Enterprise_WBG.png/500px-Herald_of_Free_Enterprise_WBG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Herald_of_Free_Enterprise_WBG.png/500px-Herald_of_Free_Enterprise_WBG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Why-because graph of the capsizing of the Herald of Free Enterprise (Click to see in detail.)","link":"https://e